\f0\fs28 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your results suggest a broadly 
\f1\b ethical, humble, and people-aware leadership profile
\f0\b0 , with one notable tension: you may sometimes rely on strategic calculation, guardedness, or political realism more than your values and empathy would ideally permit. The key development opportunity is not to suppress strategic thinking, but to make it more transparent, participative, and consistently aligned with your ethical standards.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Important context:
\f0\b0  This is a developmental interpretation, not a clinical or personality diagnosis. Scores depend heavily on the questionnaire, its norms, your work context, and how you interpreted each item. A score of 57 does not automatically mean \'93high\'94 unless the instrument\'92s validated comparison group says so. Treat the profile as a set of hypotheses to test through feedback and observed behaviour.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 1. Interpretation of your profile\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Overall leadership style\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Your likely default style is 
\f1\b principled, modest, and considerate
\f0\b0 , combined with a moderate capacity for political awareness and strategic manoeuvring.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Humility, 82:
\f0\b0  You are likely comfortable acknowledging limitations, learning from others, and avoiding excessive self-promotion.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ethical leadership, 79:
\f0\b0  You probably place substantial importance on fairness, responsibility, consistency, and the wider consequences of decisions.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Empathy, 64:
\f0\b0  You are reasonably attentive to other people\'92s needs and perspectives, although empathy may become less accessible when you are pressured, disappointed, or focused on results.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Machiavellianism, 57:
\f0\b0  You may be more politically perceptive, calculating, or sceptical about motives than your outwardly humble style suggests.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narcissism, 46:
\f0\b0  Recognition and status probably matter to you, as they do to most leaders, but they do not appear to dominate the profile.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sadism, 43:
\f0\b0  There may be some capacity for severity, enjoyment of competitive dominance, or emotional distancing, but it is not the most prominent element here.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Psychopathy, 39:
\f0\b0  Callousness, impulsive risk-taking, and lack of remorse do not appear to be central tendencies.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Workplace research links stronger dark-triad tendencies with relational, self-control, and performance risks, especially in environments with weak accountability. However, traits interact with other characteristics and context, rather than operating as simple labels. Your high humility, ethics, and moderate-to-high empathy are therefore important parts of the interpretation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11939815/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov]}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mdpi.com/2076-328X/15/3/297"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 [mdpi.com]}}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Likely leadership pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 You may come across as:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 approachable but discerning;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 modest but more ambitious than you visibly communicate;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 collaborative until you believe a decision must be made;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ethically serious, yet willing to think several moves ahead;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 empathetic, but capable of becoming emotionally detached when performance, fairness, or credibility is at stake.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This can be an effective combination. Humility makes learning easier, ethical leadership supplies boundaries, empathy supports relationships, and strategic awareness helps you navigate complex institutions. The risk is that 
\f1\b your strategic side may sometimes operate privately
\f0\b0 , while your ethical and humble side defines how you see yourself publicly.\
That gap does not imply dishonesty. It means you may occasionally rationalise a tactical behaviour because the objective seems legitimate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 Possible biases\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. The \'93good intentions\'94 bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Because you see yourself, probably accurately, as ethical and considerate, you may judge your own actions through your intention while others judge them through their impact.\
Possible manifestation:\
\'93I did this to protect the team, so the way I did it was justified.\'94\
The corrective question is:\
\'93Would the affected person describe both my objective and my process as fair?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 2. Strategic attribution bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Your Machiavellianism score may indicate greater sensitivity to informal influence, competing agendas, hidden incentives, or political behaviour. That can be valuable, but it can also lead you to interpret ambiguity as manoeuvring.\
Possible manifestation:\
\'93They are resisting because they want control.\'94\
Alternative explanations might include lack of information, workload, professional disagreement, fear, or a different understanding of the goal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 3. Humility becoming under-assertion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 High humility can occasionally make leaders reluctant to claim authority, state their contribution, challenge stronger personalities, or advocate visibly for their team.\
Possible manifestation:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 letting others define the narrative;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 delaying a difficult decision;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 giving away so much credit that your own accountability becomes unclear;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 expecting good work to speak for itself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa372\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 4. Ethical certainty\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 A strong ethical identity can produce confidence that one\'92s preferred solution is morally superior. Under pressure, disagreement may then feel like irresponsibility rather than legitimate difference.\
Watch for thoughts such as:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93Any reasonable person would agree.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93They clearly do not care about fairness.\'94\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93There is no ethical ambiguity here.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

